    "semantics": "Poisson regression of count on o3_lag02_10, adjusted for pm25_lag02_10, no2_lag02_10, a cubic B-spline of tmean_lag03 with 4 degrees of freedom (R splines::bs, interior knots at the type-7 quantiles, boundary at the range) and holiday, with one stratum per value of `stratum` absorbed by the conditional Poisson likelihood; a stratum with no events is dropped. Rows in date order; a row missing any model column is left out. Model-based errors from the inverse information; HAC errors Newey-West with Bartlett weights and 14 lags over the date-ordered rows, without small-sample correction.",
    "equivalentTo": "statsmodels: smf.glm('count ~ o3_lag02_10 + pm25_lag02_10 + no2_lag02_10 + bs(tmean_lag03, df=4) + holiday + C(stratum)', family=Poisson()).fit(cov_type='HAC', cov_kwds={'maxlags': 14}); fixed effects for the strata give the conditional model's slopes. R: gnm(..., eliminate = stratum) with sandwich::NeweyWest(lag = 14, prewhite = FALSE).",
